# 🎬 CineScope

A premium movie discovery and analytics platform powered by OMDB API.

## ✨ Features

### 🔍 Search & Discovery
- **Smart Search**: Search by movie title, actor ("starring [name]"), or director ("directed by [name]")
- **Live Autocomplete**: Get instant suggestions as you type
- **Infinite Scroll**: Seamlessly load more results as you browse
- **Recently Viewed**: Quick access to your viewing history

### 📊 Analytics Dashboard
View comprehensive statistics about your movie viewing habits:
- **Overview Stats**: Total viewed, watchlist count, favorite genre, average runtime
- **Genre Distribution**: Interactive doughnut chart showing your genre preferences
- **Viewing Timeline**: Track how many movies you've watched over time
- **Rating Distribution**: See the quality of movies you're watching
- **Decade Breakdown**: Discover which eras you prefer
- **Top Lists**: Directors, actors, and highest-rated movies you've viewed
- **Data Export**: Download your data as JSON or CSV

### ⚖️ Movie Comparison
Compare movies side-by-side to make better viewing decisions:
- **Manual Search**: Search and select 2-3 movies to compare
- **Quick Compare**: Select movies directly from your watchlist
- **Detailed Comparison**: View ratings, runtime, cast, box office, awards, and more

### 📺 Streaming Availability
Find where to watch your favorite movies:
- **Search Integration**: Check streaming options for any movie
- **Watchlist Batch Check**: See where all your watchlisted movies are available
- **Service Filter**: Browse movies by streaming platform
- **Real-time Data**: Connect to Streaming Availability API for up-to-date info

### 🔧 Advanced Filters
Fine-tune your search results with powerful filters:
- **Sort Options**: By title, year, or rating (ascending/descending)
- **Minimum Rating**: Filter by IMDB score (7.0+, 8.0+, 9.0+)
- **Decade**: Browse by era (2020s, 2010s, 2000s, etc.)
- **Runtime**: Short (<90min), Medium (90-120min), or Long (>120min)
- **Type**: Movies only or TV series only

### 🎨 UI/UX Features
- **Dark Mode**: Toggle between light and dark themes
- **Responsive Design**: Beautiful on all devices
- **Modern Cinema Aesthetic**: Premium design with elegant typography
- **Smooth Animations**: Delightful micro-interactions
- **Persistent Cache**: Fast loading with 7-day cache

## 🚀 Getting Started

### Prerequisites
- A modern web browser
- OMDB API key (included: `5e5feec5`)
- (Optional) Streaming Availability API key for streaming features

### Installation

1. Download or clone this repository
2. Open `index.html` in your web browser
3. Start searching for movies!

### Optional: Streaming Availability Setup

To enable real streaming data:

1. Sign up at [RapidAPI - Streaming Availability](https://rapidapi.com/movie-of-the-night-movie-of-the-night-default/api/streaming-availability)
2. Copy your API key
3. Navigate to the **Streaming** page in CineScope
4. Paste your API key and click "Save Key"
5. Now you can check real streaming availability!

## 📁 Project Structure

```
cinescope/
├── index.html          # Main search page
├── analytics.html      # Analytics dashboard
├── compare.html        # Movie comparison tool
├── streaming.html      # Streaming availability checker
├── style.css          # Modern cinema aesthetic styles
├── omdb.js            # Main search & filter logic
├── analytics.js       # Analytics & charts
├── compare.js         # Comparison functionality
├── streaming.js       # Streaming availability
└── README.md          # This file
```

## 🎯 Usage Guide

### Basic Search
1. Type a movie name in the search bar
2. Select from autocomplete suggestions or press Enter
3. Browse results in an elegant grid layout
4. Click any movie for detailed information

### Advanced Search
- **Search by Actor**: Type "starring Tom Hanks"
- **Search by Director**: Type "directed by Christopher Nolan"

### Using Advanced Filters
1. Click "🔍 Advanced Filters" button
2. Select your filter criteria
3. Click "Apply Filters"
4. Results will update based on your selections

### Viewing Analytics
1. Navigate to the **Analytics** page
2. View your statistics and charts
3. Explore top lists (directors, actors, ratings)
4. Export your data as JSON or CSV

### Comparing Movies
1. Navigate to the **Compare** page
2. Search for movies using the input fields
3. Click "Compare Movies"
4. Or select movies from your watchlist for quick comparison

### Managing Your Watchlist
1. Click any movie to view details
2. Click "Add to Watchlist"
3. Access your watchlist via the ⭐ button in the navbar
4. Compare watchlist movies or check streaming availability

## 🛠️ Technologies Used

- **HTML5**: Semantic markup
- **CSS3**: Modern styling with CSS Grid, Flexbox, and animations
- **JavaScript (ES6+)**: Vanilla JS for all functionality
- **Chart.js**: Beautiful, responsive charts
- **OMDB API**: Movie data
- **LocalStorage**: Client-side data persistence
- **Google Fonts**: Playfair Display & DM Sans

## 🎨 Design Philosophy

CineScope features a **Modern Cinema Aesthetic**:
- Deep blacks inspired by cinema screens
- Gold/amber accents reminiscent of film reels
- Sophisticated typography (Playfair Display + DM Sans)
- Smooth, cinematic transitions
- Card-based layouts with depth
- Elegant data visualizations

## 📊 Data & Privacy

- All data is stored locally in your browser (LocalStorage)
- No server-side storage or data collection
- Your API keys are stored locally and never transmitted to any server except the streaming API
- Cache expires after 7 days automatically

## 🔄 Future Enhancements

Potential features for future versions:
- [ ] Trailer integration (YouTube API)
- [ ] Personal rating & review system
- [ ] AI-powered movie recommendations
- [ ] Social features (share watchlists)
- [ ] Advanced statistics (viewing patterns, mood tracking)
- [ ] Collections (custom movie lists)
- [ ] PWA support (offline mode)

## 🐛 Known Limitations

- OMDB API doesn't support direct genre search (client-side filtering required)
- Streaming availability requires external API key
- Cache limited to 7 days
- Advanced filters require fetching full movie details (slower for large result sets)

